course: dictionary
lesson: 9199
title: Words with feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you about a person's character as well as what they do. «Dad's a big softie — he cried at the film.» A softie is a kind, gentle person who is easily moved. Dad cried, so the word shows he has soft feelings.
explain: Softie is informal, so you hear it in everyday talk more than in school books. It can be loving or teasing. «Not bad, ya sap» shows Cian teasing Tadhg, but the word sap is said fondly. The tone and the words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Context clues help here. Jake's dog Diesel is huge and scruffy, and everyone crosses the road. Then the sentence says that with Jake he is a big softie who sleeps on his feet. The contrast tells you softie means gentle, not tough, even though Diesel looks fierce.
fact: Softie is a noun: a softie, several softies.
fact: Softy is another spelling of the same word.
fact: «Softie» means a kind, gentle person who is easily moved, or someone who is not tough and gives in easily.
fact: «Sap» is Irish slang for a softie or a fool, and it can be said fondly.
fact: Informal words suit talk and stories, but are not always right for formal writing.
exercise: «Dad's a big softie — he cried at the film.» What does softie mean here? | A very large, strong person | A person who is always cross | *A kind person who is easily moved | A person who never shows feelings
exercise: Diesel is huge and scruffy, but he is a big softie with Jake. What does softie suggest about Diesel? | Very hungry all the time | *Gentle and friendly underneath | Lazy, and never moves | Fierce, so everyone runs away
exercise: «Not bad, ya sap.» Which word is Irish slang for a softie or a fool, said fondly? | *sap | ya | bad | not
test: Nia says her brother is a softy who cries at cartoons. Is softy the same word as softie? | *Yes, it is another spelling of the same word | Yes, but it means very strong | No, it is a different word with a different meaning | No, it means a sweet treat
test: Why does the author call Diesel a softie, even though he is huge? | Because he is a brave guard dog | Because he is huge and fierce | *Because the sentence shows he is gentle with Jake | Because everyone crosses the road to avoid him
exam: What does the word softie tell you about Diesel in «a big softie who sleeps on his feet»? | Fierce and hard to please | Very quick and sporty | Noisy whenever strangers arrive | *Gentle and affectionate with his owner
